<%#
  views/partials/header.ejs

  The site header on every page: the site name (a link to the home page) and the login
  state on the right.
  - A guest sees "Log in".
  - A logged-in user sees their name, a link to their own area (/reporter or /editor,
    chosen by their role) and a "Log out" button.

  Where currentUser comes from: middleware/setCurrentUser.js puts the session user
  ({ id, role, displayName }, or null for a guest) in res.locals.currentUser on every request,
  so every view has it without each controller passing it. The role shown here only decides
  which link to show; it protects nothing. Every protected page and API checks the role
  again on the server (requireLogin / requireRole), so a hidden link is never the protection.

  Logging out is a plain HTML form that POSTs to /logout: it works on every page even with
  JavaScript turned off, and POST (not a GET link) means another website can't log a reader
  out just by linking to us (see controllers/authController.js, logOut).

  The display name is printed with the escaping tag, so a name containing HTML is shown as text.
  The site name is the page's h1; each page's own title is an h2 below it.

  Included by: every page view. Styles: site-header, site-title, site-nav, inline-form in
  public/css/main.css.
  Owner: SH (layout). The login state and the logout form are a contract with OS.
%>
<header class="site-header">
    <h1 class="site-title"><a href="/">The Daily Web</a></h1>
    <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Account">
        <% if (currentUser) { %>
            <span>Welcome, <%= currentUser.displayName %></span>
            <% if (currentUser.role === 'reporter') { %>
                <a href="/reporter" class="btn btn-primary">My articles</a>
            <% } else if (currentUser.role === 'editor') { %>
                <a href="/editor" class="btn btn-primary">Editor area</a>
            <% } %>
            <form method="post" action="/logout" class="inline-form">
                <button type="submit" class="btn btn-danger">Log out</button>
            </form>
        <% } else { %>
            <span>Welcome, Guest</span>
            <a href="/login" class="btn btn-primary">Log in</a>
        <% } %>
    </nav>
</header>
